  "articleBody": "A successful vanity replacement starts with accurate measurements, a confirmed plumbing layout, selected fixtures, and a written scope of work. Before construction begins, clear the room, document existing conditions, verify the new vanity’s dimensions, and ask the remodeling team how plumbing, electrical work, finishes, permits, and final inspection will be handled.",
